# Registers RuntimeSecretContractGate as an environment post-processor, which is what makes a
# deployed instance refuse to start on an incomplete secret contract.
#
# spring.factories rather than a META-INF/spring/*.imports file: Spring Boot 4 loads environment
# post-processors through SpringFactoriesEnvironmentPostProcessorsFactory and has no imports-file
# path for this extension point, so an .imports file here would be a registration that silently
# registers nothing — a gate with full test coverage and no effect on any deployment.
# RuntimeSecretContractStartupTests exists because that is exactly what happened on the first
# attempt, and it caught it.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.thaap.payments.config.RuntimeSecretContractGate
